- Abram, this is a great question.

00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:35.561
I think we can get very
detailed for the VaynerNation

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:36.658
on this.

00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:39.034
Hashtag culture is very
very important specifically

00:01:39.034 --> 00:01:40.707
to Instagram and Twitter.

00:01:40.707 --> 00:01:41.948
Let's start there.

00:01:41.948 --> 00:01:44.297
That is really the two
places it is massive

00:01:44.297 --> 00:01:46.634
and on some level, Pinterest as well.

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:48.727
Less on Facebook.

00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:51.266
Tumblr, for a while there
it was very very important.

00:01:51.266 --> 00:01:53.359
Snapchat, not at all.

00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:56.243
LinkedIn, not really.

00:01:56.243 --> 00:02:01.039
We're really talking
Twitter and Instagram,

00:02:01.039 --> 00:02:02.866
first and foremost.

00:02:02.866 --> 00:02:04.818
There's another question that's
going to be on the episode,

00:02:04.818 --> 00:02:08.047
in a couple of questions where
the guy used 17, 18 hashtags

00:02:08.047 --> 00:02:09.631
as his entire post.

00:02:09.631 --> 00:02:12.863
I think hashtags are an
incredible way to get discovered,

00:02:12.863 --> 00:02:16.009
I think it's important to
think about it two ways.

00:02:16.009 --> 00:02:20.380
I think you're asking, how do
I get my hashtag going, right?

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:21.518
I think.

00:02:21.518 --> 00:02:23.123
Even if not, by answering
that it's going to help

00:02:23.123 --> 00:02:24.934
a lot of people here.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:29.931
I have the #AskGaryVee
hashtag, #AskGaryVee,

00:02:29.931 --> 00:02:32.532
Gary Vee Show I use on
Instagram and Twitter.

00:02:32.532 --> 00:02:35.154
I'm really just using that
for fans that are looking

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.450
to go down the rabbit hole
more than getting it away

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.526
for awareness.

00:02:38.526 --> 00:02:40.788
You're saying for a campaign,
and I think people really need

00:02:40.788 --> 00:02:41.766
to understand a couple of things.

00:02:41.766 --> 00:02:44.235
Number one, hashtags are not ownable.

00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:49.074
Let's just, I'm going
for, podcast listeners,

00:02:49.074 --> 00:02:50.802
I'm going for a big dramatic pause here.

00:02:50.802 --> 00:02:52.123
You should have seen the way I reacted.

00:02:52.123 --> 00:02:53.689
I'm going to do it again.

00:02:54.942 --> 00:02:56.507
It's important that you understand this.

00:02:56.507 --> 00:02:58.621
It is insane to me that
people in 2015 still think

00:02:58.621 --> 00:02:59.951
they can own a hashtag.

00:02:59.951 --> 00:03:02.725
I walk into tons of meetings
where the brand's like,

00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:05.723
let's own the hashtag #GetEm.

00:03:05.723 --> 00:03:08.485
I'm like, what the hell
are you talking about?

00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:10.863
First and foremost, any
hashtag you can create,

00:03:10.863 --> 00:03:13.077
tomorrow I can jump in and make a hashtag.

00:03:13.077 --> 00:03:17.465
We can remember all the way to
the infamous 2008 or '9 time

00:03:17.465 --> 00:03:20.472
when Skittles put out that
hashtag and then people started

00:03:20.472 --> 00:03:23.479
putting things that were
very crude against it,

00:03:23.479 --> 00:03:27.075
because Skittles homepage
was a filter and a stream

00:03:27.075 --> 00:03:29.940
of everybody using the
hashtag and then, you know,

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.292
body parts and rude and crude
things started showing up

00:03:33.292 --> 00:03:37.335
on their corporate page
because there is no ownability

00:03:37.335 --> 00:03:38.819
around a hashtag.

00:03:38.819 --> 00:03:41.561
My answer is this, flip it.

00:03:41.561 --> 00:03:45.990
Instead of trying to own
or establish a hashtag

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.993
for a campaign, look at the
hashtags that are trending

00:03:49.993 --> 00:03:53.162
and very popular on the
two main platforms already

00:03:53.162 --> 00:03:55.946
and try to figure out
how to reverse into them

00:03:55.946 --> 00:03:58.953
by putting out your piece of
content, storytelling, and then

00:03:58.953 --> 00:04:02.264
using three or four hashtags
that are riding the wave.

00:04:02.264 --> 00:04:03.626
I wrote about this a million years ago,

00:04:03.626 --> 00:04:05.043
riding the wave of a hashtag.

00:04:05.043 --> 00:04:06.674
One of my first Mediums, I think.

00:04:06.674 --> 00:04:09.436
That's the answer.

00:04:09.436 --> 00:04:12.910
Reverse it, don't try to establish one,

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:15.227
ride the wave of four or
five that are working,

00:04:15.227 --> 00:04:18.559
that tie in and be creative
into what you're putting out.

